{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Every firstborn of your sons you shall redeem, and they shall not appear before Me empty.</b> One who merits being a firstborn — this is a great distinction, and it alludes to the Holy One, blessed be He, for He is the firstborn of the world. And the sacrificial service from eternity belonged to the firstborn. Therefore Jacob our father was zealous for it, and Esau the wicked, who despised the service of HaShem, sold it. Afterward the firstborn were disqualified through the sin of the calf, and the Levites were set apart in their place, so that the service would be in them and not in the firstborn. And even though the service is no longer in them, they still retain a distinction and superiority over other people by virtue of being firstborn. Our Rabbis of blessed memory expounded: Every matter concerning which it is said 'to Me' — it is in this world and in the world to come. Israel are in this world and in the world to come, as it is said (Leviticus 26:26) ״ואבדיל אתכם מן העמים להיות לי״. The Levites, as it is said (Numbers 3:45) ״והיו לי הלוים״. The Land, as it is said (Exodus 19:5) ״כי לי כל הארץ״. The firstborn, as it is said (Numbers 3:13) ״כי לי כל בכור״ — in this world and in the world to come; end of quotation. And the commandment of the firstborn does not apply to females but only to males, as it is said (Exodus 13:13) ״פטר כל רחם בבני ישראל״, and it is written (ibid.) ״וכל בכור אדם בבניך תפדה״. And the firstborn must hold fast to Torah and fear of Heaven more than other people, by virtue of the distinction in him that he is a firstborn. And his father must fulfill the commandment of his redemption, for it is a commandment incumbent upon the father; if the father did not redeem him, he is obligated to redeem himself. And if he is unredeemed, whether on account of his father or on account of himself, he is punished, for thus our Rabbis of blessed memory expounded: Why was the going up for the festival juxtaposed to the redemption of the firstborn? To tell you that the firstborn who were redeemed receive the countenance of the Shekhinah and merit seeing the building of the Holy Temple, may it be built speedily in our days; but if they were not redeemed, they shall not see."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {0 "Citation 'Leviticus 26:26' is the printed reference; the verse quoted (ואבדיל אתכם מן העמים להיות לי) is actually Leviticus 20:26 — retained the author's (or edition's) citation as written per the exact-numbers rule."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:07:03.667300539Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}